{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27456393","formula":"C₂₉H₃₉ClN₇O₂P","hill":"C29H39ClN7O2P","elements":["H","C","N","O","P","Cl"],"composition":{"C":29.0,"H":39.0,"N":7.0,"O":2.0,"P":1.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Brigatinib"},"descriptions":{"en":"Brigatinib, sold under the brand name Alunbrig among others, is a small-molecule targeted cancer therapy being developed by Ariad Pharmaceuticals, Inc. Brigatinib acts as an inhibitor of the receptor tyrosine kinase anaplastic lymphoma kinase (ALK) and epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR), as well as several nonreceptor tyrosine kinases such as FAK, FAK2, and FER. It shows activity against ALK-positive non–small cell lung cancer, ALK-positive anaplastic large cell lymphoma (ALCL), and NF2-related schwannomatosis. Brigatinib could overcome resistance to osimertinib conferred by the EGFR C797S mutation if it is combined with an anti-EGFR antibody such as cetuximab or panitumumab."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":68165256,"mass":584.1,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1CCN(CC1)C2CCN(CC2)C3=CC(=C(C=C3)NC4=NC=C(C(=N4)NC5=CC=CC=C5P(=O)(C)C)Cl)OC","inchikey":"AILRADAXUVEEIR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"5-chloro-4-N-(2-dimethylphosphorylphenyl)-2-N-[2-methoxy-4-[4-(4-methylpiperazin-1-yl)piperidin-1-yl]phenyl]pyrimidine-2,4-diamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"68165256","atoms":79,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-10.774,"y":-1.259,"z":1.134,"el":"C"},{"x":-9.664,"y":-0.368,"z":1.452,"el":"N"},{"x":-9.453,"y":0.613,"z":0.373,"el":"C"},{"x":-8.048,"y":1.259,"z":0.404,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.915,"y":0.302,"z":0.309,"el":"N"},{"x":-7.368,"y":-1.068,"z":0.627,"el":"C"},{"x":-8.425,"y":-1.109,"z":1.755,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.168,"y":0.412,"z":-0.968,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.45,"y":1.78,"z":-1.103,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.951,"y":1.685,"z":-0.8